---
id: PY-001
type: rule
family: python-reliability
title: '# type: ignore without an error code'
version: 1

severity: warning
confidence: high
spectrum_position: 4

targets: [source]
file_extensions: [.py]
allowlist: ['**/test_*.py', '**/*_test.py', '**/tests/**', '**/conftest.py', '**/explain/**']

detection:
  type: regex
  pattern: '#\s*type:\s*ignore([^\[]|$)'

related: [PY-002, PY-003]
enabled: true
opt_in: false
---

A blanket `# type: ignore` silences every type error on this line, including
ones a later edit introduces. Scope it to the failure you actually mean to
suppress: `# type: ignore[assignment]`. If the whole line is genuinely
un-typeable, suppress with a reason instead:
`# @anvil-ignore PY-001 -- third-party stub is wrong, see upstream #123`.
